en features quartz countertops, stainless steel appliances, a large island, and expansive windows with ocean views. One bedroom/family room has been converted to an ADU with a separate entrance; it includes a cozy fireplace, French doors opening to a private patio, built-in cabinets, a small fridge, and a remodeled private bath. The main-level powder room was remodeled in 2025. The large primary suite has a private bath and a separate entrance to the backyard; two additional bedrooms share a Jack-and-Jill bath. Other updates include air conditioning, a newer heater (2023), a new roof (2024) using original tiles with new underlayment, and a whole-house water filtration system. The attached two-car garage offers additional storage. The home is partially remodeled and freshly painted in most rooms. Located in Palos Verdes Estates, known for top-rated schools, dramatic coastline, community events, and a charming small downtown with restaurants, a grocery market, a coffee shop, and an artisan creamery.","Spanish Tile","Family Room, Jack & Jill, Kitchen, Laundry, Living Room, Primary Suite, Separate Family Room, Walk-In Closet","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","Lunada Bay","Palos Verdes","Palos Verdes","","","","","","","","","","False","Full Service","Easy to show.  Please call/text Listing Agent Cheryl at 3108729098. First showing at Brokers Open House April 7, 11:00 to 1:30.","True","None","False","","3412","Assessor","","CA","Active","Multi/Split ","","","Via Sanchez","","2520","","","Contemporary","Conventional","","6890","","Single Family Residence","","Cable Connected, Electricity Connected, Sewer Connected, Water Connected","Neighborhood, Ocean, Panoramic, Water","True","","","Drapes","1974","90274","2806","PVR1*"
