 Security System","Assessor","","","SB25278581","","3","3","","1","Owner","Denise","","424.206.6441","","Driveway, Garage, Garage - Three Door, Gated, Private","True","Stone","True","75","","Private, In Ground","True","","1132.15","Old-world Tuscan charm meets elevated coastal living in a home that knows how to make an entrance?and then casually steals the show. With nearly 6,500 sq ft of light-filled living, this Palos Verdes Estates beauty delivers grand scale without a hint of stiffness. Think impressive, inviting, and surprisingly easy to live in. The main level includes a chef?s kitchen where weeknight dinners turn into lingering conversations?and full-blown celebrations feel effortless. Quartzite countertops, an oversized island, dual sinks, triple Wolf ovens, and multiple Sub-Zero refrigerators make hosting feel natural, while the fully equipped butler?s pantry (yes, it has its own Wolf oven and wine fridge) keeps things running smoothly behind the scenes. Custom barn doors add a touch of charm, and statement chandeliers and tray ceilings bring just the right amount of drama. Walls of glass frame sweeping ocean and city coastal views which flood the home with sunshine, while architectural moments?like the show-stopping spiral staircase?deliver wow factor in all the right places. Five generously sized en-suite bedrooms (four of them conveniently located on the main level) ensure comfort and privacy for everyone, and the primary suite feels like a private spa escape you?ll look forward to retreating to every night. A rich, wood-clad English pub brings a cozy old-soul vibe?perfect for laid-back evenings and well-earned nightcaps. Plus, the main floor offers easy access to nearly every corner of the home plus the backyard, making indoor-outdoor living a breeze. Step outside and the vibe shifts to full-on resort mode. Spanning nearly 19,000 sq ft, the grounds feature a pool and spa, outdoor kitchen with built-in BBQ, fire pit, multiple patios for gathering, and grassy spaces perfect for play, lounging, or sunset toasts. When it?s time to switch gears, the elevator makes heading downstairs effortless, whether you?re settling in for movie night in the private theater, hosting guests in the guest bedroom, or breaking a sweat in the flexible bonus room?currently living its best life as a gym. The expansive front lawn creates a grand arrival, but it?s the sweeping coastline views and iconic Queen?s Necklace from both levels that really steal the spotlight?especially when the lights start to sparkle. Designed for unforgettable moments, easy entertaining, and everyday living that feels a little more magical?this is one home that knows how to have a good time (and look very good doing it).","Spanish Tile, Tile","Bonus Room, Center Hall, Entry, Exercise Room, Family Room, Galley Kitchen, Guest/Maid's Quarters, Home Theatre, Kitchen, Laundry, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Main Floor Primary Bedroom, Primary Bathroom, Primary Bedroom, Primary Suite, Media Room, Utility Room, Walk-In Closet","","Palos Verdes Peninsula Unified","","","","","","","","","","","","","False","Full Service","By private showing only. Contact Ed Kaminsky 310.427.2414 or Denise Feneht for showings 424.206.6441.","","Private, In Ground","True","","6349","Assessor","","CA","Active","Two","","","Via La Brea","","2232","","","Mediterranean, Spanish","Cash, Cash to New Loan, Conventional","","7330","","Single Family Residence","","Sewer Connected","City Lights, Coastline, Mountain(s), Neighborhood, Ocean","True","https://www.zillow.com/view-imx/46db59d6-0c3a-479d-973e-bbfd11d9bb18?wl=true&setAttribution=mls&initialViewType=pano","https://media.zillowmediaexperts.com/sites/jggxzqv/unbranded","Blinds, Double Pane Windows","2008","90274","","PVR1YY"
