perfecting the connection of steel sash windows, and designing sliding glass-and-steel doors so guests could drift between the living room and patio without spilling a drop of their drink.  When the HOA insisted on Spanish tile roofs, Neutra politely disagreed? and found a way to make it work anyway, designing parapets that kept his modernist vision intact. Acting as his own general contractor, he chased bids for everything from major steelwork to the andirons by the fireplace, because no detail was too small for his obsession. This isn?t just a home?it?s a living piece of architectural art with the Pacific Ocean as your backdrop and a designer who thought of everything so you wouldn?t have to.","Tile","Bonus Room, Family Room, Kitchen, Living Room, Main Floor Bedroom, Main Floor Primary Bedroom","","Palo Verde Unified","","","","","","","","","","","","","False","Full Service","Please call John Corrales at 310.346.3332","True","","","","1668","Assessor","","CA","Active","One","","","Via Montemar","","1400","","","Contemporary","Conventional","","6884","","Single Family Residence","","","Ocean, Panoramic","True","https://dan-solomon-photo.aryeo.com/sites/weozqob/unbranded","https://dan-solomon-photo.aryeo.com/sites/weozqob/unbranded","","1940","90274","1265","PVR1YY"
